# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
#
# Advisory clang-tidy profile for the target code of a product: Zephyr adapters, devicetree-bound
# drivers and the product's own sources that a Zephyr build compiles. It is not named .clang-tidy,
# so clang-tidy never picks it up by itself. check_target_tidy.py passes it with --config-file.
# To run clang-tidy by hand: clang-tidy -p build --config-file=style/target.clang-tidy <file>
#
# Advisory means findings are reported and no run fails because of one: WarningsAsErrors is empty,
# unlike style/.clang-tidy, which is Crux's gating selection. There is no HeaderFilterRegex here.
# The script computes one from the Git top level of the product, so nothing needs editing.
#
# The selection equals Crux's .clang-tidy, a test compares the two, with one exception:
#   -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters
# A Zephyr driver API fixes parameter lists such as (dev, reg, value) that the product cannot
# change, so this check is expected to report them. That is a reading of the check, not a
# measurement: nobody has run this profile on Zephyr driver sources. Remove the exception if a
# real run shows no noise, and add others the same way, with the reason beside them.
#
# readability-identifier-naming has no options, so it reports nothing, as in Crux's own file. The
# naming rules of docs/coding-guidelines.md in Crux are not enforced by this file.
Checks: >-
  -*,
  bugprone-*,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  -clang-analyzer-security.insecureAPI.DeprecatedOrUnsafeBufferHandling,
  performance-*,
  -performance-enum-size,
  portability-*,
  readability-identifier-naming
WarningsAsErrors: ''
...
